WEBVTT

00:01.209 --> 00:06.208
A DAIEI PRESENTATION

00:13.968 --> 00:15.468
"Once upon a time,

00:15.548 --> 00:21.309
in a forest lived a man
and his beautiful daughter.

00:22.689 --> 00:24.149
One day,

00:24.859 --> 00:29.109
a golden carriage drawn by six
horses stopped before their house.

00:30.028 --> 00:32.238
Out of the carriage stepped a king.

00:32.738 --> 00:38.658
'Would you give me your daughter
to be my wife?' he asked the man.

00:39.698 --> 00:44.789
Delighted, the man agreed.

00:45.668 --> 00:49.298
Truth be told, the king was very handsome,

00:49.959 --> 00:53.298
his only flaw being his
beard, which was blue.

00:54.628 --> 00:59.808
Apart from this, there was
no fault to be found with him."

01:03.189 --> 01:05.019
BLUEBEARD

01:05.099 --> 01:08.608
-What is it?
-Nothing.

01:20.698 --> 01:24.829
Enough of the book.
Let's talk about something else.

01:25.668 --> 01:26.998
Yes, please.

01:27.079 --> 01:29.088
-Feeling all right?
-Yes.

01:35.679 --> 01:37.009
I know how

01:38.009 --> 01:39.968
the story ends.

01:42.098 --> 01:47.188
In the end, the daughter kills Bluebeard.

02:58.468 --> 03:00.679
-You are?
-Takabe, from headquarters.

03:00.758 --> 03:02.848
Thank you for coming.

03:02.929 --> 03:06.308
Mr. Takabe, do you want to see the cleaner

03:06.389 --> 03:08.808
-who found the body?
-No.

03:09.978 --> 03:14.228
A prostitute. Something like this
was bound to happen someday.

03:15.528 --> 03:18.899
-I'm Takabe.
-Yasukawa, from the precinct.

03:19.528 --> 03:21.949
-Find anything?
-Yes.

03:59.778 --> 04:05.329
If it was this Kuwano
guy, he took off in the raw.

04:05.989 --> 04:10.118
And he left us his ID.

04:13.628 --> 04:14.959
Excuse me.

04:23.298 --> 04:28.348
She was struck with a blunt object,
but she died from loss of blood.

04:29.178 --> 04:31.889
It wouldn't have taken long.

04:32.558 --> 04:36.858
Both carotid arteries
have been neatly severed.

04:37.728 --> 04:41.569
Have you ever seen wounds like this before?

04:41.649 --> 04:42.858
No.

04:43.488 --> 04:44.608
I see.

04:45.369 --> 04:49.158
But the perp is no ordinary character.

04:50.288 --> 04:54.869
You don't have to go this
far just to kill someone.

04:57.418 --> 05:01.379
The suspect may have
a motorcycle or a bicycle.

05:02.048 --> 05:06.048
Check all the service roads.
I'm on my way.

05:17.059 --> 05:20.028
I'm going to check out his neighborhood.
You want to come?

05:37.418 --> 05:39.668
Takabe, here.

05:45.968 --> 05:49.259
Then there was blood everywhere.

05:50.598 --> 05:51.808
Lots of it.

05:51.889 --> 05:55.228
Sakuma, this came from
the Shibaura Precinct.

06:02.028 --> 06:03.278
And then

06:03.899 --> 06:08.278
I looked at her face —

06:10.699 --> 06:13.538
He looks okay to me.

06:18.829 --> 06:22.879
They've requested a psychiatrist.

06:22.959 --> 06:24.879
What's the point?

06:26.928 --> 06:28.759
So he's like the rest?

06:29.259 --> 06:33.889
Yep. Admits intent, then says
afterwards he was stunned.

06:35.808 --> 06:39.558
The devil made them
do it is all I can guess.

06:45.149 --> 06:46.858
Three cases in two months.

06:48.608 --> 06:50.199
What's going on?

06:50.988 --> 06:53.028
The media doesn't know?

06:53.119 --> 06:56.619
No. We haven't released any details.

06:57.658 --> 06:59.668
No TV or book plots like this?

07:00.209 --> 07:01.999
None. We checked.

07:02.588 --> 07:05.088
No leaks, either.

07:06.209 --> 07:10.678
Unless you've said something
in one of your lectures.

07:10.759 --> 07:12.468
Give me a break!

07:12.548 --> 07:16.809
The perps aren't related in any
way and they're all perfectly rational.

07:17.889 --> 07:21.309
-So it just happened.
-"Just happened"?

07:23.478 --> 07:26.728
People like to think a
crime has some meaning.

07:27.399 --> 07:29.858
But most of them don't.

07:35.699 --> 07:38.619
So somebody "just happened" to do this?

09:03.619 --> 09:05.119
Where is this?

09:07.129 --> 09:08.629
Shirasato Beach.

09:35.149 --> 09:36.489
Where is it?

09:36.989 --> 09:38.739
Shirasato Beach.

09:38.828 --> 09:39.908
Where?

09:40.408 --> 09:42.538
Shirasato, in Chiba.

09:42.619 --> 09:45.959
Shirasato? Where's that?

09:46.499 --> 09:48.328
Where are you going?

09:49.629 --> 09:50.838
Nowhere.

10:40.389 --> 10:41.719
Yes?

10:41.798 --> 10:43.219
What's the date?

10:43.889 --> 10:45.479
February 26th.

10:48.229 --> 10:49.479
Where is this?

10:49.979 --> 10:51.609
I just told you.

10:51.688 --> 10:53.938
When was that?

10:54.438 --> 10:56.188
Just over there.

10:56.899 --> 11:00.739
Uh, do you know who I am?

11:01.239 --> 11:02.369
What?

11:03.448 --> 11:06.908
I don't know who I am.

11:08.249 --> 11:09.749
You what?

11:14.298 --> 11:15.759
Help me.

11:16.259 --> 11:17.759
Please.

11:19.048 --> 11:20.759
I don't remember anything.

11:25.639 --> 11:28.729
-Could he use a drink?
-No, coffee's fine.

11:29.808 --> 11:30.979
Here.

11:35.818 --> 11:39.649
What's that sound out there?

11:43.619 --> 11:44.869
The waves.

11:51.369 --> 11:53.038
It's so quiet.

11:58.668 --> 12:03.639
"Mamiya" is written here.
Could that be your name?

12:05.139 --> 12:06.509
I don't know.

12:07.139 --> 12:09.678
You could be "Mr. Mamiya."

12:11.308 --> 12:12.729
Mamiya?

12:14.979 --> 12:19.438
That's fine. Mamiya can be my name.

12:20.818 --> 12:22.528
It probably is.

12:23.528 --> 12:26.119
Maybe we should ask the police.

12:27.448 --> 12:29.658
No. No police.

12:29.749 --> 12:31.158
Why not?

12:41.418 --> 12:43.178
Then let's talk some more.

12:43.928 --> 12:46.469
Perhaps your family, your work.

12:48.769 --> 12:50.558
First tell me about yourself.

12:52.519 --> 12:53.849
Me?

12:54.349 --> 12:58.568
I teach elementary school and I'm married.
That's it.

12:59.688 --> 13:01.278
Where's your wife?

13:01.778 --> 13:03.278
Sleeping upstairs.

13:04.198 --> 13:06.158
Why is she doing that?

13:06.239 --> 13:07.619
She has a cold.

13:08.869 --> 13:09.908
Who does?

13:17.038 --> 13:18.208
Mr. Mamiya.

13:19.958 --> 13:21.129
Mr. Mamiya.

13:22.719 --> 13:23.838
Who's that?

13:24.379 --> 13:26.389
You, Mr. Mamiya.

13:36.399 --> 13:42.239
Well, I've told you about me.
Now you tell me about you.

13:43.489 --> 13:44.989
About me?

13:45.908 --> 13:47.318
Anything.

13:47.989 --> 13:50.698
Doesn't the name Mamiya
bring back anything?

13:52.908 --> 13:54.038
No.

13:55.999 --> 13:57.879
Why were you on the beach?

13:58.418 --> 14:01.208
-Where?
-Shirasato Beach.

14:04.379 --> 14:07.259
I don't know what you're talking about!

14:10.349 --> 14:12.469
Okay, let's talk about something else then.

14:12.558 --> 14:14.599
I want to hear about you.

14:15.269 --> 14:17.308
I've already told you.

14:20.229 --> 14:21.568
Yeah?

14:23.729 --> 14:25.649
I don't remember.

14:28.908 --> 14:32.698
I teach school.
There's just me and my wife.

14:34.408 --> 14:36.209
What does your wife do?

14:36.288 --> 14:38.538
Nothing. She's a housewife.

14:39.038 --> 14:40.418
Who is?

14:40.499 --> 14:42.209
My wife.

14:46.418 --> 14:51.469
Oh, the woman in the pink negligee...

14:54.058 --> 14:55.599
You saw her?

14:56.849 --> 15:02.318
I don't remember anything. You do.

15:13.658 --> 15:18.749
Tell me more about your wife.

15:30.178 --> 15:32.469
I'll be right back.

15:32.548 --> 15:35.599
Hello. Could you give me a minute?

15:43.058 --> 15:44.688
Bunch of idiots!

15:45.519 --> 15:47.109
What did I do wrong?

15:47.899 --> 15:49.649
I do things my way.

15:50.359 --> 15:52.908
What? Go to hell!

15:53.948 --> 15:57.658
Damn right I'm mad!
Stop fucking around, you dumb shit!

15:57.749 --> 15:59.288
Sorry to keep you.

15:59.369 --> 16:02.379
Here we are.

16:06.668 --> 16:09.009
-There you go.
-Good. Thanks.

16:09.089 --> 16:10.969
Thank you very much.

16:11.048 --> 16:13.889
Mr. Takabe, one moment.

17:15.108 --> 17:16.739
Hello.

17:16.818 --> 17:18.828
Sorry. Did I wake you?

17:19.788 --> 17:21.249
I'll do that.

17:21.328 --> 17:22.709
No, I will...

17:22.788 --> 17:25.209
No, I feel good today.

17:35.548 --> 17:37.298
Where's the opener?

17:39.469 --> 17:40.638
Here.

17:53.318 --> 17:57.108
-I poured you some beer.
-Thanks.

18:06.499 --> 18:08.788
How's work? Busy?

18:09.538 --> 18:12.919
Yeah. How about you?

18:13.009 --> 18:17.798
Me? I just did nothing all day long.

18:33.439 --> 18:34.608
Fumie.

18:37.778 --> 18:41.368
When this case is over,
let's take a trip somewhere.

18:42.989 --> 18:44.749
Oh, that's all right...

18:44.828 --> 18:47.999
No, I'd like to go somewhere.

18:50.038 --> 18:54.509
We're definitely going. You decide where.

18:55.169 --> 18:56.628
Where?

18:56.719 --> 19:01.429
I'll leave that up to you.
Okinawa, Hokkaido, anywhere.

19:03.469 --> 19:05.888
From one extreme to the other.

19:08.229 --> 19:09.848
You decide.

19:12.058 --> 19:13.439
All right.

20:00.949 --> 20:02.739
The victim is

20:02.818 --> 20:07.409
Tomoko Hanaoka, 26, the suspect's wife.

20:07.489 --> 20:10.159
Her carotid arteries were cut.

20:12.078 --> 20:18.048
"Suspect teaches elementary school.
Committed to his work, a good teacher.

20:18.878 --> 20:23.719
High school classmates, married two years.

20:23.798 --> 20:26.138
Neighbors describe them as a fine couple.

20:27.259 --> 20:29.769
No trouble with debt or anything."

20:30.519 --> 20:32.769
The devil made him do it?

20:57.419 --> 20:58.628
Mr. Hanaoka,

20:59.338 --> 21:03.048
last night you killed your wife Tomoko.

21:04.088 --> 21:05.798
Is that correct?

21:08.098 --> 21:09.098
Mr. Hanaoka?

21:13.229 --> 21:15.019
You sliced her open with a knife

21:15.939 --> 21:20.028
from throat to chest.

21:22.568 --> 21:23.949
Why?

21:25.858 --> 21:28.028
Why did you kill her like that?

21:29.368 --> 21:32.868
I don't know. Why did I do it?

21:34.788 --> 21:38.288
Did you read some novel
or see some movie like that?

21:40.878 --> 21:42.669
Did someone talk to you?

21:44.219 --> 21:45.378
No.

21:48.219 --> 21:49.638
I see.

21:53.269 --> 21:55.729
Did you hate your wife?

21:58.898 --> 22:04.028
Things weren't going well
between you, were they?

22:04.739 --> 22:06.989
No, that's not true.

22:07.528 --> 22:09.068
Then isn't it strange?

22:11.239 --> 22:13.499
What is it, Mr. Hanaoka?

22:24.419 --> 22:26.759
I remember everything.

22:27.929 --> 22:31.888
I killed Tomoko.
At the time it just seemed

22:33.388 --> 22:35.929
the natural thing to do.

22:39.098 --> 22:42.108
-Was there a quarrel?
-No.

22:42.778 --> 22:46.068
It's weird.
You murdered your wife for no reason?

22:48.949 --> 22:52.909
That's right. There was no reason.

22:55.249 --> 23:00.249
But I killed her! I killed Tomoko!

23:04.509 --> 23:07.338
Mr. Hanaoka, crying won't help.

23:08.298 --> 23:12.098
I'm going to keep on
asking you until you tell me.

23:13.098 --> 23:16.058
-I'm sure this is hard for you —
-That's enough, Takabe.

23:16.138 --> 23:18.348
-No.
-That's enough.

23:19.808 --> 23:21.058
Take him.

23:23.608 --> 23:26.989
He's not lying. He remembers everything.

23:27.528 --> 23:30.409
Chances are he's completely sane.

23:38.999 --> 23:40.578
Hey! Stop that!

23:41.538 --> 23:47.169
Would a person cut someone up like
that because the devil made them do it?

23:55.179 --> 24:01.058
What if they all had some
similar trauma in their childhoods?

24:01.808 --> 24:06.608
It lies suppressed for
years, then they explode.

24:06.689 --> 24:08.108
Could that happen?

24:08.608 --> 24:11.699
Since when did you become a shrink?

24:12.449 --> 24:17.078
I've been reading up. You know, my wife...

24:17.828 --> 24:20.328
Don't laugh. Beginners' books.

24:21.828 --> 24:25.378
Don't believe everything you read.

24:25.878 --> 24:27.669
Well, it's in a book.

24:28.709 --> 24:32.719
No one can understand
what motivates a criminal,

24:32.798 --> 24:34.969
sometimes not even the criminal.

24:35.048 --> 24:38.388
No one understands.

24:42.808 --> 24:45.269
You're getting in too deep.

24:45.898 --> 24:51.528
No. All I want is to find words
that will explain the crimes.

24:54.028 --> 24:55.739
That's my job.

24:57.239 --> 24:59.159
Yeah, I guess so.

25:01.909 --> 25:04.959
How is your wife, by the way?

25:06.078 --> 25:09.509
She's going to the
hospital you recommended.

25:11.259 --> 25:13.469
She's a lot better.

25:14.259 --> 25:15.588
Yeah?

25:17.969 --> 25:19.929
At least, it seems that way.

25:21.348 --> 25:22.939
I don't know if she really is.

25:25.148 --> 25:27.769
-Thank you very much.
-That's all right.

25:27.858 --> 25:30.358
-I might have to come again.
-You might?

25:30.439 --> 25:33.648
Could you contact this officer
if someone else moves in?

25:33.739 --> 25:36.108
-All right.
-Give him your number.

26:36.838 --> 26:40.969
Hey, you! What are you doing up there?

26:42.509 --> 26:45.888
You'll get hurt! Come down!

26:56.398 --> 26:58.699
I'm coming up!

27:02.949 --> 27:04.328
Damn fool!

27:05.618 --> 27:08.538
Name, address and particulars unknown.

27:09.038 --> 27:13.378
He appears to be in his late 20s.

27:14.759 --> 27:17.338
Yes, I know that.

27:18.378 --> 27:20.888
All right, thank you.

27:25.179 --> 27:27.888
Well, the station is looking
for information on you,

27:28.388 --> 27:30.648
but if you yourself don't know...

27:30.729 --> 27:32.479
The computer has nothing either.

27:44.078 --> 27:47.538
Don't worry.
Tomorrow we'll get you to a hospital.

27:48.038 --> 27:49.999
Have some tea.

27:53.838 --> 27:55.709
Is this your place?

27:57.209 --> 27:59.419
No, it's a police box.

28:01.429 --> 28:03.969
-You're a cop?
-Yes.

28:10.098 --> 28:12.479
Why am I talking to you?

28:14.108 --> 28:17.108
I want to ask you some questions.

28:19.949 --> 28:21.409
About me?

28:23.489 --> 28:28.159
Do you remember standing on that roof?

28:31.618 --> 28:35.128
What about coming to
this police box with me?

28:39.128 --> 28:40.969
Is this a police box?

28:42.628 --> 28:43.888
Yes.

28:49.019 --> 28:50.598
Who are you?

28:55.229 --> 28:56.858
Oh, boy!

28:57.818 --> 28:59.479
Okay, enough.

29:02.818 --> 29:05.118
-May I smoke?
-Sure.

29:06.659 --> 29:09.999
-You can't smoke here.
-That's okay.

29:18.999 --> 29:20.128
Here.

29:21.378 --> 29:22.878
I'm on duty.

29:23.969 --> 29:25.088
Oh.

29:31.179 --> 29:33.598
-Here.
-Oh, thanks.

29:36.189 --> 29:37.979
I'll go do my rounds.

29:54.868 --> 29:56.828
It must be hard work.

29:57.328 --> 30:00.048
Sometimes.

30:19.898 --> 30:21.189
I'm sleepy.

30:23.989 --> 30:25.568
I'm gonna sleep a bit.

30:26.398 --> 30:27.568
Okay.

31:00.019 --> 31:01.269
Mr. Oida.

31:05.608 --> 31:07.148
Look at this.

31:19.328 --> 31:21.249
You hear me, don't you?

31:22.338 --> 31:23.459
Yes.

31:24.959 --> 31:26.509
You know what I'd like?

31:27.878 --> 31:29.838
I'd like to hear about you.

31:30.759 --> 31:31.969
Huh?

31:35.138 --> 31:36.638
Tell me.

31:46.989 --> 31:49.568
I think it's the flu.

31:53.989 --> 31:56.038
Does your throat hurt?

31:56.118 --> 31:57.828
A little.

32:01.118 --> 32:03.749
Lower your trousers and lie down, please.

32:03.838 --> 32:04.999
What?

32:09.838 --> 32:12.048
Lower your trousers and lie down.

32:13.179 --> 32:14.259
Okay.

32:33.909 --> 32:35.659
That's good enough.

32:39.538 --> 32:41.538
Raise your knees a bit.

32:47.709 --> 32:49.548
You're not shy, are you!

32:50.759 --> 32:52.679
Your lymph glands are a bit swollen.

32:53.179 --> 32:54.759
Fine, thank you.

33:19.409 --> 33:21.659
What do you want at this hour?

33:21.749 --> 33:23.919
Sorry. This won't take long.

33:25.788 --> 33:28.838
Ten minutes, and that's all.

33:29.878 --> 33:31.298
Listen,

33:32.009 --> 33:35.429
you don't think it might be
some kind of hypnosis, do you?

33:35.509 --> 33:36.848
Huh?

33:36.929 --> 33:40.269
You know, someone
looks at a flashing light,

33:40.348 --> 33:43.179
then does whatever someone else tells them?

33:43.269 --> 33:45.558
"Hypnotic suggestion."

33:46.648 --> 33:50.148
Is it possible? What do you think?

33:51.568 --> 33:53.818
You're the only one I dare ask.

33:55.028 --> 33:57.949
-Well?
-Got some new evidence?

33:58.489 --> 34:00.199
Just an idea.

34:02.368 --> 34:06.459
Hypnotism itself is a
very common technique.

34:07.078 --> 34:10.378
But even if you manage
to hypnotize someone,

34:10.458 --> 34:13.798
you can't change their basic moral sense.

34:14.298 --> 34:18.389
A person who thinks
murder is evil won't kill anyone

34:18.469 --> 34:20.639
under hypnotic suggestion.

34:27.768 --> 34:33.648
Could you induce someone
to cut in that "X" pattern?

34:35.699 --> 34:40.079
It would take forever to get a
suggestion like that into place.

34:40.159 --> 34:43.119
-It's impossible?
-I didn't say that.

34:43.619 --> 34:46.498
If the hypnotist was a genius...

34:47.668 --> 34:49.998
But why would someone do that?

34:51.668 --> 34:52.798
I don't know.

34:52.878 --> 34:57.969
A thrill killing? Some thrill that'd be.

34:59.548 --> 35:04.179
You said yourself that no one
knows what motivates a criminal.

35:53.608 --> 35:57.568
Mr. Oida, do you know where
the stuff for the Ward Office is?

35:57.648 --> 35:59.489
The right-hand shelf.

36:01.909 --> 36:05.079
-Yeah, here it is.
-Like I said.

36:14.248 --> 36:15.748
Be right back.

37:08.969 --> 37:09.969
Come in.

37:12.518 --> 37:14.478
Sorry I'm late.

37:14.559 --> 37:17.898
That's all right. Did something happen?

37:17.978 --> 37:20.778
-I got lost.
-Lost?

37:21.358 --> 37:22.608
Yes.

37:23.239 --> 37:25.239
Did you come another way?

37:25.778 --> 37:31.199
I don't know.
Suddenly I just didn't know where I was.

37:32.329 --> 37:34.458
How did you get here, then?

37:35.418 --> 37:36.958
I don't know.

37:38.378 --> 37:41.708
Suddenly I was in front of the hospital.

37:43.418 --> 37:47.139
Well, it all worked out for the best.
You got here.

37:47.219 --> 37:48.389
Yes.

37:49.139 --> 37:50.268
That book...

37:52.309 --> 37:55.518
It's Bluebeard. Do you remember it?

37:59.358 --> 38:01.818
No, I've never seen it before.

38:10.119 --> 38:12.449
There's nothing physically wrong.

38:13.998 --> 38:17.418
Just a sprained ankle.
Nothing to worry about.

38:19.539 --> 38:23.048
So how's your memory?

38:27.548 --> 38:33.559
Tomorrow we'll move you to a hospital
with a proper psychiatric department.

38:34.679 --> 38:35.768
Sure.

38:44.068 --> 38:49.909
How far back do you remember?

38:53.079 --> 38:56.659
I remember talking to you.

38:56.748 --> 38:57.829
Any worries?

38:57.918 --> 39:00.588
Worries? About what?

39:01.748 --> 39:03.498
You're quite calm.

39:08.219 --> 39:10.298
You're the one with worries.

39:11.219 --> 39:12.349
Sorry?

39:14.018 --> 39:15.518
May I smoke?

39:16.018 --> 39:17.809
There's no smoking here.

39:18.309 --> 39:19.559
I see.

39:26.778 --> 39:29.449
What do you mean, I have worries?

39:32.239 --> 39:34.079
Uh, what?

39:35.748 --> 39:37.079
I forget.

39:43.128 --> 39:44.378
Water.

40:21.369 --> 40:25.458
Doctor, can I tell you something?

40:27.259 --> 40:28.509
Certainly.

40:29.509 --> 40:34.048
All the things that used to be inside me,

40:34.929 --> 40:36.679
now they're all outside.

40:38.518 --> 40:39.849
So,

40:40.768 --> 40:46.148
I can see all of the
things inside you, Doctor.

40:49.318 --> 40:51.489
But the inside of me

40:53.278 --> 40:54.989
is empty.

41:28.688 --> 41:30.148
Don't look at me.

41:36.739 --> 41:39.119
Now you tell me about yourself.

41:40.659 --> 41:43.579
About me? What about me?

41:45.329 --> 41:46.998
Why you became a doctor.

41:48.128 --> 41:49.458
Why?

41:50.378 --> 41:53.668
You're just a woman.
Why did you become a doctor?

41:54.969 --> 41:56.548
Just a woman?

42:00.719 --> 42:05.268
That's what people said, isn't it?

42:07.608 --> 42:09.108
They did, didn't they?

42:10.858 --> 42:12.398
Think back.

42:13.778 --> 42:16.858
Remember exactly how you felt.

42:20.028 --> 42:21.699
Just a woman.

42:25.708 --> 42:30.798
Woman is a lower life form than man.
Isn't she?

42:37.088 --> 42:41.349
See? Now you remember.

42:43.518 --> 42:45.429
When you were in medical school,

42:47.268 --> 42:51.188
you dissected a corpse, didn't you?

42:53.648 --> 42:55.398
The first corpse you'd ever seen.

42:56.858 --> 42:58.489
It was a man, wasn't it?

43:00.659 --> 43:02.159
Think back.

43:03.909 --> 43:06.208
You'd never seen a naked man before.

43:07.918 --> 43:11.708
You took your scalpel and cut into him.

43:13.798 --> 43:18.219
It made you feel good, didn't it?

43:19.838 --> 43:21.099
Didn't it?

43:22.309 --> 43:23.429
Think back.

43:24.929 --> 43:27.349
You wanted to be a surgeon,

43:28.438 --> 43:32.978
but you weren't sure you
could, and you ended up a GP.

43:34.688 --> 43:35.858
No.

43:37.528 --> 43:42.489
What you really wanted
to do was cut a man open.

44:46.929 --> 44:49.018
You shot him in the head.

44:49.809 --> 44:51.768
Wasn't that enough?

44:54.768 --> 45:00.989
Is there a reason why you cut
into the dead man with a knife?

45:02.148 --> 45:03.278
Yes.

45:04.528 --> 45:07.829
He was someone I didn't like.

45:07.909 --> 45:09.159
Why?

45:10.498 --> 45:11.998
Many reasons.

45:13.789 --> 45:18.338
It's been three years since
he was transferred to our box.

45:19.458 --> 45:21.378
I put up with him all the time.

45:23.048 --> 45:27.389
Finally I couldn't stand it anymore.

45:27.469 --> 45:28.969
But to kill him?

45:30.059 --> 45:31.179
Yes.

45:32.099 --> 45:36.398
Detective, you've never
killed anyone, have you?

45:38.728 --> 45:42.858
That's how you get when you hate
someone from the bottom of your heart.

45:43.449 --> 45:46.199
So it was an angry impulse?

45:46.909 --> 45:49.949
No. I was completely calm.

45:53.289 --> 45:56.458
Isn't that a bit strange?

45:58.208 --> 46:01.259
Yes, it definitely is strange.

46:02.259 --> 46:03.548
May I?

46:06.389 --> 46:08.679
I'm Sakuma, a psychiatrist.

46:09.429 --> 46:14.268
Officer Oida, do you remember
seeing anything shiny?

46:14.349 --> 46:15.688
For example,

46:17.188 --> 46:18.728
something like this?

46:21.188 --> 46:22.228
No.

46:23.489 --> 46:27.199
Were you talking to
anyone before the crime?

46:28.119 --> 46:29.239
No.

46:31.489 --> 46:35.159
Is that true? Try to remember.

46:35.708 --> 46:39.458
Do you think you could
stop doing that, please?

46:39.539 --> 46:40.838
Keep going.

46:41.378 --> 46:42.918
Don't stop!

46:43.628 --> 46:47.378
You did talk to someone, didn't you?

46:47.469 --> 46:50.429
We know you did. Look at the light.

46:51.719 --> 46:53.059
No. No one.

46:53.139 --> 46:55.679
Yes, you did. Who was it?

46:55.768 --> 46:57.478
What was his name?

46:57.559 --> 46:58.688
I didn't!

47:00.858 --> 47:02.528
-Enough.
-Mr. Oida.

47:04.938 --> 47:08.858
You must have seen a light like this.

47:08.949 --> 47:10.568
Was anyone there?

47:11.949 --> 47:15.289
Someone told you to do this, didn't they?

47:16.579 --> 47:18.079
Who was it?

47:19.039 --> 47:24.838
There might have been someone there.

47:24.918 --> 47:26.918
-Was there?
-I don't know!

47:27.009 --> 47:30.639
Of course you know. Who was it?

47:31.259 --> 47:33.059
Tell me his name, please.

47:34.599 --> 47:39.309
-His name?
-Yes, his name. What was his name?

47:41.188 --> 47:44.188
He... didn't have a name.

47:44.278 --> 47:48.358
What do you mean?
Mr. Oida, look at the light.

47:48.449 --> 47:49.989
That's enough.

48:05.958 --> 48:09.128
Excuse me. I'm thirsty.

48:19.889 --> 48:21.728
It is hypnosis.

48:21.809 --> 48:24.398
We can't be sure of that.

48:24.478 --> 48:26.728
But that wasn't normal.

48:26.818 --> 48:29.108
I decide what's normal.

48:30.148 --> 48:32.028
Stop traumatizing people.

48:32.108 --> 48:37.409
Sakuma, we're not counseling
this man, we're interrogating him.

48:53.338 --> 48:54.759
-Don't move!
-But...

48:54.849 --> 48:56.259
Just stay there.

49:37.969 --> 49:40.219
Mr. Oida? Mr. Oida?

49:42.688 --> 49:45.018
What was that you just did?

49:46.188 --> 49:48.518
Just now? Nothing.

49:49.018 --> 49:51.398
What's that motion you're
making with your hand?

49:53.858 --> 49:55.108
This?

50:00.329 --> 50:01.498
I don't know.

50:03.329 --> 50:05.329
Nothing in particular.

50:05.829 --> 50:08.338
Tell me about what you just did.

50:15.219 --> 50:18.349
I was just thinking of Officer Tamura.

50:21.219 --> 50:22.728
That's all.

50:24.018 --> 50:27.728
Nothing more than that.

51:17.489 --> 51:19.949
How long will this go on?

51:21.528 --> 51:22.699
Here we go.

51:29.958 --> 51:31.128
Mr. Takabe!

51:34.208 --> 51:35.918
What are you doing?

51:36.009 --> 51:39.429
Another murder. The restrooms
in Chuo Park. Get over there.

51:39.509 --> 51:45.139
There was a report of a suspicious
person at Shiomicho Hospital.

51:45.719 --> 51:47.849
Oida took him in there.

52:00.858 --> 52:02.739
-Amnesia?
-Apparently.

52:02.829 --> 52:05.619
-Where is he?
-He's not in his room.

52:06.289 --> 52:08.958
-So where is he?
-They say he hasn't left.

53:08.309 --> 53:10.309
I know you're here.

53:20.528 --> 53:23.028
Step out here, please.

53:24.278 --> 53:27.199
-Where?
-Here.

53:27.989 --> 53:31.329
I don't know where "here" is.

53:31.409 --> 53:35.039
Well, then, I'll have to come to you.

53:48.259 --> 53:49.429
Where are you?

53:51.639 --> 53:52.889
Come out.

53:54.559 --> 53:56.099
Who are you?

54:00.278 --> 54:01.778
Police.

54:02.278 --> 54:03.449
Who?

54:04.398 --> 54:05.949
A police officer.

54:08.619 --> 54:10.909
Do you understand my question?

54:13.039 --> 54:15.998
I've got some questions to ask you.

54:20.458 --> 54:22.759
I want to hear about you.

54:22.838 --> 54:25.719
I ask the questions! You answer!

54:27.509 --> 54:29.009
Who are you?

54:30.139 --> 54:31.309
Where are you?

54:32.679 --> 54:35.599
-Who are you?
-A detective!

54:37.398 --> 54:39.228
Stop screwing around!

54:50.159 --> 54:51.659
Name?

54:54.199 --> 54:55.708
I forget.

54:58.539 --> 55:00.708
Address? Age? Occupation?

55:02.918 --> 55:04.259
Don't know.

55:08.088 --> 55:10.259
When were you checked in?

55:12.559 --> 55:14.018
Where?

55:14.099 --> 55:15.889
The hospital.

55:16.889 --> 55:18.438
Shiomicho Hospital.

55:19.059 --> 55:22.608
You saw Dr. Miyajima.

55:25.818 --> 55:26.949
Where?

55:30.119 --> 55:31.659
We're going in circles.

55:54.059 --> 55:57.018
Have you ever met any of these people?

55:59.978 --> 56:01.309
I don't remember.

56:07.858 --> 56:10.778
How about this person?

56:16.329 --> 56:17.498
I don't know.

56:18.829 --> 56:21.079
This is you.

56:39.059 --> 56:40.268
It looks like me.

56:40.768 --> 56:43.358
So now we're sure of one thing.

56:43.858 --> 56:46.068
That's you. All right?

56:47.528 --> 56:49.358
I don't know him.

56:51.278 --> 56:52.778
So this is me?

56:59.159 --> 57:00.409
Who are you?

57:02.539 --> 57:05.168
A detective. How about these?

57:11.429 --> 57:12.628
Corpses.

57:15.048 --> 57:17.309
-Do you like these?
-No.

57:19.179 --> 57:22.768
If you don't like them,
why do you have them?

57:23.349 --> 57:24.728
It's my job.

57:26.188 --> 57:27.318
Job?

57:29.648 --> 57:31.188
What's your job?

57:32.858 --> 57:35.568
Right now, asking you questions.

57:37.449 --> 57:38.579
Why?

57:39.369 --> 57:42.659
You're an important source of information.

57:43.998 --> 57:46.918
Me? Why?

57:50.548 --> 57:54.469
We found your fingerprints
at the Hanaoka house.

57:54.548 --> 58:00.139
Whether you remember or not, you know him.

58:03.099 --> 58:06.518
Oh, is that what you mean?

58:09.478 --> 58:11.438
You know a lot, Detective.

58:12.398 --> 58:14.989
Not what's inside your head.

58:16.818 --> 58:17.989
My head?

58:25.289 --> 58:26.458
Here?

58:30.298 --> 58:34.259
Your attitude isn't helping you at all.

58:35.088 --> 58:36.259
Why?

58:38.298 --> 58:41.139
Right. I want you to try and
remember from the beginning.

58:42.179 --> 58:47.478
You admit you were in Shiomicho Hospital?

58:48.099 --> 58:51.398
What's wrong?
Why are you raising your voice?

58:52.438 --> 58:54.068
Because you won't answer.

58:54.148 --> 58:57.159
-Why?
-Answer my questions.

58:57.239 --> 58:58.659
May I smoke?

59:02.119 --> 59:03.789
-No.
-Takabe.

59:09.958 --> 59:11.128
Detective?

59:12.548 --> 59:13.668
Yes?

59:15.628 --> 59:18.969
Tell me more about yourself.

59:21.259 --> 59:22.889
After you talk.

59:23.389 --> 59:25.929
Stop it! Leave him alone!

59:34.938 --> 59:37.699
I need to examine him,

59:37.778 --> 59:41.199
but I see clear symptoms
of typical psychosis.

59:42.659 --> 59:44.159
Don't get into it with him.

59:46.248 --> 59:47.708
You'll just get angry.

59:57.918 --> 01:00:00.389
Hey, you all right?

01:00:01.179 --> 01:00:02.849
Yeah. I'm all right.

01:01:21.298 --> 01:01:25.599
I went out to the convenience
store, and I got lost.

01:01:27.259 --> 01:01:28.389
I see.

01:01:29.889 --> 01:01:31.978
We'll need toothbrushes.

01:01:32.809 --> 01:01:35.059
We will, won't we?

01:01:36.438 --> 01:01:40.438
What if we stay at a hotel

01:01:40.528 --> 01:01:44.068
where they don't give you one?

01:01:50.998 --> 01:01:55.378
I'll do the shopping, okay?

01:01:58.998 --> 01:02:02.168
You're tired.

01:02:03.628 --> 01:02:05.679
You don't have to do everything for me.

01:02:09.469 --> 01:02:13.268
We don't have to take a trip, either.

01:02:17.608 --> 01:02:21.398
We'll take that trip. Definitely.

01:02:23.818 --> 01:02:25.568
My next holiday.

01:02:32.699 --> 01:02:33.789
For sure.

01:02:35.539 --> 01:02:36.668
Hey.

01:02:37.168 --> 01:02:39.378
Impound all that guy's stuff.

01:02:39.458 --> 01:02:43.469
But he's a witness, not a suspect.

01:02:43.548 --> 01:02:45.469
I don't care. The works.

01:03:00.978 --> 01:03:02.438
What's that?

01:03:02.528 --> 01:03:05.858
A scar from a burn. Not very old.

01:03:06.358 --> 01:03:09.369
Possibly caused by contact with metal.

01:03:10.239 --> 01:03:12.329
Something round and hot.

01:03:12.909 --> 01:03:14.409
Round and hot.

01:03:46.898 --> 01:03:48.199
This way.

01:04:04.458 --> 01:04:06.298
No one's home.

01:04:06.378 --> 01:04:08.418
-Do you have the key?
-Yeah.

01:04:11.969 --> 01:04:14.759
Is Mr. Mamiya in some kind of trouble?

01:04:15.268 --> 01:04:17.099
That's what I'm here to find out.

01:04:17.179 --> 01:04:19.688
I see. Well, it's all yours.

01:04:21.938 --> 01:04:23.108
Excuse me.

01:04:24.268 --> 01:04:26.778
When did you last see Mr. Mamiya?

01:04:27.438 --> 01:04:30.778
About six months ago, maybe.

01:04:31.278 --> 01:04:33.449
I don't come out here much.

01:04:33.949 --> 01:04:36.289
He paid a year's rent in advance.

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:39.039
I'll be downstairs if you need me.

01:05:04.268 --> 01:05:07.978
SEVERE PERSONALITY DISORDERS:
PSYCHOTHERAPEUTIC STRATEGIES

01:05:10.028 --> 01:05:13.318
PSYCHODYNAMIC PSYCHOTHERAPY
OF BORDERLINE PATIENTS

01:05:15.159 --> 01:05:17.869
THE THEORY OF PSYCHOANALYSIS
BY CARL GUSTAV JUNG

01:05:27.128 --> 01:05:29.708
PERSONALITY DISORDER

01:05:32.759 --> 01:05:34.259
MESMERISM AND THE END

01:05:34.260 --> 01:05:35.759
OF THE ENLIGHTENMENT IN FRANCE

01:05:36.679 --> 01:05:39.679
MESMER, OU L'EXTASE MAGNÉTIQUE

01:05:55.528 --> 01:05:58.619
ANIMAL MAGNETISM
AND ITS PSYCHOLOGICAL EFFECTS

01:06:02.208 --> 01:06:03.893
KUNIHIKO MAMIYA

01:06:03.894 --> 01:06:05.579
MUSASHINO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY

01:06:20.768 --> 01:06:22.639
MAY CAUSE A "SPASM"...

01:06:22.728 --> 01:06:24.559
FALLS INTO A COMA...

01:06:24.639 --> 01:06:27.228
MESMERISM

01:07:15.989 --> 01:07:19.409
Sakuma, I've found out who our man is.

01:07:20.579 --> 01:07:22.619
Kunihiko Mamiya.

01:07:22.699 --> 01:07:26.159
A psychology student
up until three years ago.

01:07:27.289 --> 01:07:31.378
His professors said he
hardly showed up for classes.

01:07:32.378 --> 01:07:34.298
Yeah, just like you.

01:07:34.878 --> 01:07:39.469
Then he was a live-in part-timer
at a junkyard in Kawasaki.

01:07:40.798 --> 01:07:43.259
That's probably where he got burned.

01:07:44.139 --> 01:07:45.849
Vanished six months ago.

01:07:47.268 --> 01:07:50.268
No, I don't know what he was doing.

01:07:52.478 --> 01:07:56.148
Have you ever heard of Mesmer?

01:08:02.869 --> 01:08:05.449
Okay. Tell me when I get back.

01:09:19.069 --> 01:09:22.779
What's wrong? What happened?

01:09:27.868 --> 01:09:31.118
Don't scare me like that. Are you ill?

01:09:32.918 --> 01:09:34.578
Why are you home now?

01:09:36.788 --> 01:09:38.498
It's nothing.

01:09:39.168 --> 01:09:42.179
He's ill. I've moved him to the hospital.

01:09:42.259 --> 01:09:45.009
-On whose authority?
-My own.

01:09:45.599 --> 01:09:48.389
-Are you trying to take him away from me?
-That's right.

01:09:48.469 --> 01:09:51.809
It's dangerous to let you
keep talking to that man.

01:09:53.269 --> 01:09:54.849
You bastard.

01:09:55.979 --> 01:09:59.819
-Hey! What about Mesmer?
-I'll ask him.

01:10:09.738 --> 01:10:11.448
No one's supposed to see him.

01:10:13.328 --> 01:10:14.498
Open up.

01:10:25.639 --> 01:10:26.798
Move.

01:10:46.158 --> 01:10:49.448
What's wrong? Your hands are shaking.

01:10:56.998 --> 01:10:58.328
I found out.

01:11:00.248 --> 01:11:04.798
Your name is Kunihiko Mamiya.

01:11:06.628 --> 01:11:07.929
Is that right?

01:11:08.009 --> 01:11:12.309
Mamiya, who is this man called Mesmer?

01:11:13.269 --> 01:11:14.429
Who?

01:11:15.059 --> 01:11:16.439
Mesmer.

01:11:18.189 --> 01:11:21.729
At the university you studied about Mesmer

01:11:22.229 --> 01:11:24.439
and hypnotic suggestion.

01:11:25.529 --> 01:11:26.698
What?

01:11:28.029 --> 01:11:30.118
Whether you remember or not,

01:11:30.948 --> 01:11:36.618
I'm going to have you arraigned
on charges of incitement to murder.

01:11:38.708 --> 01:11:40.498
It's over.

01:11:46.548 --> 01:11:49.219
You saw your wife dead, didn't you?

01:11:57.059 --> 01:11:59.729
Your wife is ill, isn't she?

01:12:02.479 --> 01:12:04.859
Is it hard caring for her at home?

01:12:07.738 --> 01:12:10.988
Where did you hear about that?

01:12:12.198 --> 01:12:14.658
The other detective told me.

01:12:18.708 --> 01:12:22.288
Does it bother you,
talking about your wife?

01:12:29.759 --> 01:12:33.599
Anyway, there'll be lots of time.

01:12:35.429 --> 01:12:37.599
You can't get out of here.

01:12:38.099 --> 01:12:41.849
-It's you who wants out.
-I know what you did.

01:12:41.939 --> 01:12:46.229
Tell me whatever you like.
That's why you came, isn't it?

01:12:50.149 --> 01:12:55.529
You planted hypnotic suggestions
in those people's minds.

01:12:55.618 --> 01:12:59.118
It's hard to be a
detective with a crazy wife.

01:12:59.208 --> 01:13:00.248
Shut up.

01:13:00.328 --> 01:13:05.088
You do it by keeping your work and
your family life completely separate.

01:13:05.168 --> 01:13:06.878
How did you do it?

01:13:06.958 --> 01:13:11.929
The detective or the
husband, which is the real you?

01:13:12.009 --> 01:13:14.179
How did you hypnotize them?

01:13:14.259 --> 01:13:16.509
Neither one is the real you.

01:13:17.469 --> 01:13:19.679
There is no real you.

01:13:21.019 --> 01:13:22.559
Your wife knows that, too.

01:13:22.649 --> 01:13:24.559
How did you hypnotize them?

01:13:26.439 --> 01:13:27.609
Watch.

01:13:32.149 --> 01:13:33.448
You're right.

01:13:34.448 --> 01:13:38.988
My wife is a burden. I know.
You don't have to tell me!

01:13:41.288 --> 01:13:42.708
I'm a detective.

01:13:43.458 --> 01:13:47.918
I've been taught never to show
emotion, even with my family.

01:13:47.998 --> 01:13:51.009
And this is the result.

01:13:56.389 --> 01:13:58.599
I don't understand her.

01:13:59.179 --> 01:14:02.229
She doesn't understand what I go through.

01:14:02.809 --> 01:14:06.479
I know it's my fault that it's that way.
So what?

01:14:06.559 --> 01:14:08.019
What else could you do?

01:14:08.109 --> 01:14:11.189
That's right! What other way is there?

01:14:14.908 --> 01:14:15.988
Look,

01:14:17.029 --> 01:14:21.408
you think this is how I wanted to end up?

01:14:21.908 --> 01:14:26.628
We should all relax, enjoy
ourselves, lead peaceful lives.

01:14:26.708 --> 01:14:28.538
But society isn't like that!

01:14:29.838 --> 01:14:33.798
Oh, so society's to blame.

01:14:34.798 --> 01:14:36.759
It's people like you.

01:14:37.849 --> 01:14:44.389
It's guys like you who have
my head about to split open!

01:14:46.729 --> 01:14:51.899
Lunatics like you have it easy
while citizens like me go through hell!

01:14:53.149 --> 01:14:57.198
I spend my whole life taking
care of that wife of mine!

01:15:14.048 --> 01:15:15.628
If it weren't for you...

01:15:18.759 --> 01:15:21.759
things would be fine with my wife and me.

01:15:26.439 --> 01:15:28.439
Her I can forgive...

01:15:30.859 --> 01:15:33.149
but you I can't.

01:15:43.578 --> 01:15:45.078
You're amazing.

01:15:55.298 --> 01:15:57.418
You like that? Hearing me talk?

01:15:58.378 --> 01:15:59.509
Yeah.

01:16:03.139 --> 01:16:04.559
Good.

01:16:06.019 --> 01:16:08.139
Now it's your turn.
I want the whole story.

01:16:10.149 --> 01:16:11.979
All of it.

01:16:16.738 --> 01:16:17.859
What's wrong?

01:16:22.158 --> 01:16:24.288
Can't talk without your lighter?

01:16:30.248 --> 01:16:31.328
Here.

01:16:40.509 --> 01:16:42.298
You're amazing.

01:17:37.109 --> 01:17:42.279
The water will make you calm.

01:17:46.908 --> 01:17:51.158
It will make you happy, empty.

01:17:53.918 --> 01:17:58.418
You'll be born again, just like me.

01:18:18.689 --> 01:18:20.279
Are you all right?

01:18:21.359 --> 01:18:22.439
Was it you?

01:18:24.149 --> 01:18:26.408
Did you tell him about me?

01:18:27.069 --> 01:18:31.578
Uh, well, you know, he keeps
asking all these questions...

01:18:44.009 --> 01:18:47.639
Mesmer was an 18th-century
Austrian doctor,

01:18:48.599 --> 01:18:50.889
the first man to study hypnosis.

01:18:52.519 --> 01:18:55.979
It wasn't recognized then
as a medical treatment.

01:18:56.769 --> 01:19:01.069
They saw it as fakery, magic,

01:19:01.569 --> 01:19:03.109
or witchcraft.

01:19:05.109 --> 01:19:06.408
And?

01:19:06.488 --> 01:19:09.658
There's still a lot we
don't know about Mesmer.

01:19:10.488 --> 01:19:13.748
Some say he really did
study magic and alchemy.

01:19:16.538 --> 01:19:18.918
And Mamiya's doing that?

01:19:19.538 --> 01:19:21.128
Impossible.

01:19:22.088 --> 01:19:26.719
If so, the diagnosis would be simple.

01:19:27.469 --> 01:19:31.469
He'd simply be a megalomaniac.

01:19:33.179 --> 01:19:34.389
But that's not it.

01:19:35.309 --> 01:19:39.729
He has definitely lost his memory,
but otherwise he's not abnormal.

01:19:40.859 --> 01:19:45.899
But he's also a man with
a very complex personality.

01:19:47.859 --> 01:19:50.819
I see. Okay.

01:19:57.828 --> 01:19:59.078
Takabe.

01:20:00.958 --> 01:20:02.628
Don't talk to him.

01:20:03.708 --> 01:20:05.668
You don't know what could happen.

01:20:07.338 --> 01:20:08.548
Don't get in too deep.

01:20:10.469 --> 01:20:11.639
I know.

01:20:46.798 --> 01:20:47.798
Takabe.

01:20:55.099 --> 01:21:00.809
Mr. Mamiya, could you tell
us your name or date of birth?

01:21:01.809 --> 01:21:03.809
Anything you remember.

01:21:10.319 --> 01:21:11.488
Well?

01:21:12.029 --> 01:21:15.738
Do you remember anything about yourself?

01:21:19.448 --> 01:21:20.498
No.

01:21:21.288 --> 01:21:22.498
Mr. Mamiya,

01:21:23.498 --> 01:21:27.668
are you aware of the
situation you are in at present?

01:21:29.969 --> 01:21:32.548
I mean the charges against you.

01:21:34.889 --> 01:21:36.179
Who are you?

01:21:37.219 --> 01:21:39.139
Fujiwara, from headquarters.

01:21:40.639 --> 01:21:42.059
Well, Mr. Mamiya?

01:21:43.269 --> 01:21:47.569
Do you understand why you're here now?

01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:49.479
What?

01:21:49.569 --> 01:21:52.109
Don't ask questions, answer them.

01:21:52.198 --> 01:21:53.488
What questions?

01:21:53.988 --> 01:21:55.118
Mr. Mamiya,

01:21:56.328 --> 01:22:00.198
incitement to murder can
carry the death penalty.

01:22:00.908 --> 01:22:03.418
Do you understand that?

01:22:03.498 --> 01:22:05.328
Is that your boss?

01:22:05.828 --> 01:22:06.998
Yes.

01:22:09.338 --> 01:22:10.838
That must be a drag.

01:22:10.918 --> 01:22:13.969
Mr. Mamiya, answer my question.

01:22:14.969 --> 01:22:16.298
Who are you?

01:22:17.599 --> 01:22:20.429
-Fujiwara. Headquarters.
-Who?

01:22:20.519 --> 01:22:22.769
-Are you being smart?
-Who are you?

01:22:26.149 --> 01:22:29.189
Takabe, what's wrong with this man?

01:22:29.689 --> 01:22:32.319
-I'm asking who you are.
-Answer my question!

01:22:33.279 --> 01:22:36.819
All right, I'll ask you again.

01:22:38.698 --> 01:22:40.658
Fujiwara-of-Headquarters.

01:22:42.158 --> 01:22:43.458
Who are you?

01:22:46.168 --> 01:22:49.878
What... exactly do you mean?

01:22:51.918 --> 01:22:53.918
You think about that.

01:23:00.349 --> 01:23:01.599
I'm very sorry!

01:23:02.559 --> 01:23:05.769
You must understand, he has amnesia.

01:23:08.899 --> 01:23:10.729
What a bunch.

01:23:14.899 --> 01:23:17.109
They don't understand, do they?

01:23:19.238 --> 01:23:20.618
About me,

01:23:21.618 --> 01:23:22.998
or about you.

01:23:27.708 --> 01:23:32.208
Detective, do you hear my voice?

01:23:35.338 --> 01:23:36.719
You do, don't you?

01:23:39.429 --> 01:23:43.809
That proves you're a special person.

01:23:47.599 --> 01:23:49.479
You knew that from the start.

01:23:52.019 --> 01:23:53.689
So did I.

01:23:55.899 --> 01:23:57.988
You're different from them.

01:24:02.279 --> 01:24:03.618
You're someone

01:24:04.868 --> 01:24:09.458
who can understand what I'm really saying.

01:24:16.378 --> 01:24:17.378
Take him away.

01:26:34.689 --> 01:26:36.609
Will Okinawa be warm?

01:26:40.229 --> 01:26:41.988
Let's eat lots of good food.

01:26:44.779 --> 01:26:47.118
What do you want to eat?

01:26:49.948 --> 01:26:53.498
Fumie, we're not going to Okinawa.

01:26:55.078 --> 01:26:56.168
I know.

01:27:05.128 --> 01:27:09.759
The sea there must be beautiful.

01:27:15.729 --> 01:27:18.399
Just until my work settles down.

01:27:19.689 --> 01:27:21.109
I understand.

01:27:21.689 --> 01:27:22.979
I'll take her bag.

01:27:24.069 --> 01:27:25.569
Shall we go?

01:27:30.828 --> 01:27:33.328
Thank you, Doctor.

01:27:36.118 --> 01:27:37.578
Mr. Takabe.

01:27:39.668 --> 01:27:42.168
It's not good to work too hard.

01:27:44.668 --> 01:27:49.048
You look sicker than your wife to me.

01:27:55.639 --> 01:27:59.939
I'm sorry, I don't have the tag.
I wonder where it went.

01:28:00.439 --> 01:28:03.779
-A week ago, wasn't it?
-Yes.

01:28:05.319 --> 01:28:06.859
Mr. Takabe?

01:28:06.948 --> 01:28:09.109
One moment, please.

01:28:27.588 --> 01:28:29.798
I'm sorry, sir, but it's not here.

01:28:30.838 --> 01:28:32.679
That can't be.

01:28:34.509 --> 01:28:37.139
Maybe you took it somewhere else?

01:28:37.229 --> 01:28:38.349
No.

01:28:38.439 --> 01:28:40.559
Or you gave it to your wife.

01:28:40.649 --> 01:28:41.899
No.

01:28:51.908 --> 01:28:53.488
May I take your plate?

01:28:55.328 --> 01:28:56.538
Yes.

01:29:06.548 --> 01:29:07.708
Yeah?

01:29:09.048 --> 01:29:10.259
Sakuma?

01:29:11.929 --> 01:29:13.088
What?

01:29:15.009 --> 01:29:16.599
No, I'm not busy.

01:29:18.559 --> 01:29:19.559
Now?

01:29:26.189 --> 01:29:28.319
I want to show you something.

01:29:28.988 --> 01:29:30.149
What?

01:29:30.238 --> 01:29:34.529
A film on hypnotherapy.
The university put it on video.

01:29:37.578 --> 01:29:43.168
The oldest material on hypnotism in Japan.

01:29:45.128 --> 01:29:49.458
It probably dates from
the end of the 19th century.

01:30:00.769 --> 01:30:03.059
Watch the man's hand.

01:30:06.609 --> 01:30:10.529
You have to look closely. See? There.

01:30:11.319 --> 01:30:14.158
You see what looks like an X?

01:30:28.418 --> 01:30:30.668
-That's it?
-Yeah.

01:30:31.759 --> 01:30:33.009
What does it mean?

01:30:33.929 --> 01:30:38.759
Her name was Suzu Murakawa.
She was treated for hysteria.

01:30:39.349 --> 01:30:41.309
That's all that's recorded.

01:30:43.639 --> 01:30:46.019
Police records say...

01:30:48.149 --> 01:30:54.399
she was arrested for the
murder of her son in 1898.

01:30:57.279 --> 01:31:01.078
She seems to have killed him

01:31:01.618 --> 01:31:06.248
by carving the shape
of a cross into his neck.

01:31:08.538 --> 01:31:10.458
That's all we know.

01:31:12.048 --> 01:31:14.469
Did Mamiya see this film?

01:31:15.219 --> 01:31:16.548
I don't know.

01:31:17.298 --> 01:31:21.099
There's not much chance even
medical students would see it.

01:31:22.389 --> 01:31:26.229
But even if he had,

01:31:27.559 --> 01:31:32.229
that still wouldn't explain his actions.

01:31:37.029 --> 01:31:39.529
Who's this man in the film?

01:31:40.868 --> 01:31:42.038
Unknown.

01:31:43.078 --> 01:31:48.538
We do know, however, why he
didn't show his face to the camera.

01:31:51.288 --> 01:31:56.378
You know what they called
hypnotism in Japan back then?

01:31:59.338 --> 01:32:00.679
"Soul conjuring."

01:32:01.759 --> 01:32:05.729
Like clairvoyance,
spiritualism — that sort of thing.

01:32:07.809 --> 01:32:13.439
The authorities in any age
always suppress occultism...

01:32:15.779 --> 01:32:20.618
and the Meiji government back then
would have suppressed this technique.

01:32:21.779 --> 01:32:27.618
It would only have been
performed in secret ceremonies.

01:33:13.628 --> 01:33:16.668
HERESIES

01:33:22.389 --> 01:33:26.509
CHAPTER 4 — MESMER

01:33:28.979 --> 01:33:32.519
TOJIRO HAKURAKU DOB UNKNOWN,
DIED IN 1898

01:35:18.628 --> 01:35:19.788
Sakuma.

01:35:30.009 --> 01:35:31.009
Huh?

01:35:31.969 --> 01:35:35.229
So what is Mamiya, then?

01:35:37.189 --> 01:35:40.059
What's your guess? Tell me.

01:35:42.189 --> 01:35:43.529
A missionary.

01:35:44.819 --> 01:35:46.149
A missionary?

01:35:47.609 --> 01:35:50.988
Sent to propagate the ceremony.

01:35:56.288 --> 01:35:59.578
Sorry, I was just imagining things.

01:36:01.838 --> 01:36:04.048
What am I saying?

01:36:04.668 --> 01:36:07.679
Don't take me seriously.

01:36:09.259 --> 01:36:10.889
I'm a little tired.

01:36:12.509 --> 01:36:14.559
Let's call it a day.

01:36:15.309 --> 01:36:18.349
Now I'm getting in too deep.

01:36:28.149 --> 01:36:31.368
Sakuma, what's that?

01:36:39.918 --> 01:36:42.458
Oh, that?

01:36:43.338 --> 01:36:46.759
I just thought it might help me to think.

01:36:47.259 --> 01:36:48.588
About what?

01:36:49.798 --> 01:36:52.469
About...

01:36:55.179 --> 01:36:56.469
I don't know.

01:37:03.109 --> 01:37:05.149
You met Mamiya, didn't you?

01:37:05.229 --> 01:37:06.479
No.

01:37:08.359 --> 01:37:09.448
Yes, you did.

01:37:11.408 --> 01:37:12.738
It's weird.

01:37:14.988 --> 01:37:16.448
I don't remember.

01:39:18.529 --> 01:39:21.578
Kunihiko Mamiya's whereabouts unknown.

01:39:21.658 --> 01:39:28.038
Earlier reports of him near
Kawasaki Station were inaccurate.

01:39:28.538 --> 01:39:31.548
In the absence of further information,

01:39:31.628 --> 01:39:36.179
the search area is being
widened from Tokyo and Saitama

01:39:36.259 --> 01:39:39.048
to the entire Kanto plain.

01:39:40.389 --> 01:39:41.509
Hello?

01:39:42.469 --> 01:39:44.389
One moment, please.

01:39:45.269 --> 01:39:47.269
Mr. Takabe, it's for you.

01:39:48.769 --> 01:39:49.939
Hello?

01:39:51.939 --> 01:39:53.439
I see.

01:39:55.109 --> 01:39:57.238
We're on our way.

01:40:23.309 --> 01:40:26.599
Dr. Sakuma's body has
been taken to the hospital.

01:40:28.019 --> 01:40:32.399
It was probably suicide.
He strangled himself.

01:40:34.569 --> 01:40:36.738
He'd cuffed himself to that pipe,

01:40:37.649 --> 01:40:39.158
strange as that sounds.

01:43:40.878 --> 01:43:43.168
So you've come, Detective.

01:43:56.139 --> 01:43:58.019
Why did you let me escape?

01:44:03.149 --> 01:44:04.569
You know why?

01:44:06.319 --> 01:44:11.948
By letting me escape, you
could learn my true secret.

01:44:13.578 --> 01:44:15.158
All by yourself.

01:44:19.998 --> 01:44:22.248
You didn't have to, though.

01:44:24.668 --> 01:44:30.639
Anyone who wants to meet his
true self is bound to come here.

01:44:31.679 --> 01:44:33.389
It's fate.

01:44:53.868 --> 01:44:55.118
Remember now?

01:44:57.118 --> 01:44:59.958
Do you remember everything?

01:45:08.088 --> 01:45:09.259
You do?

01:45:11.679 --> 01:45:15.139
This is the end for you, too.

01:46:27.798 --> 01:46:30.548
Fearsome... heart of...

01:46:31.219 --> 01:46:33.298
His... healing hand.

01:46:33.378 --> 01:46:36.639
Road of healing... Not a long...

01:46:36.719 --> 01:46:39.349
Take sword...

01:46:39.849 --> 01:46:43.189
A man... but dew.

01:46:43.269 --> 01:46:48.569
Heal, O... water grass! O winter...

01:46:48.649 --> 01:46:50.149
falls... snow.

01:46:50.229 --> 01:46:51.738
That... heal... snow.

01:46:51.819 --> 01:46:54.198
Take... in hand... heal.

01:47:26.849 --> 01:47:28.359
Shall I bring your coffee?

01:47:33.738 --> 01:47:34.859
Yes?

01:47:37.738 --> 01:47:41.408
All right. Bring the car around.

01:48:01.309 --> 01:48:02.639
Here you are.

01:48:03.389 --> 01:48:05.139
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

01:49:12.788 --> 01:49:15.548
KOJI YAKUSHO

01:49:15.628 --> 01:49:18.338
TSUYOSHI UJIKI

01:49:18.418 --> 01:49:20.969
ANNA NAKAGAWA

01:49:21.759 --> 01:49:23.219
YUKIJIRO HOTARU

01:49:23.298 --> 01:49:24.509
YORIKO DOGUCHI

01:49:24.599 --> 01:49:25.889
DENDEN

01:49:25.969 --> 01:49:27.269
REN OSUGI

01:49:27.349 --> 01:49:28.929
MASAHIRO TODA

01:49:29.019 --> 01:49:30.519
AKIRA OTAKA

01:49:30.599 --> 01:49:31.939
TOSHI KATO

01:49:47.118 --> 01:49:49.538
MASATO HAGIWARA

01:49:51.828 --> 01:49:53.998
EXECUTIVE PRODUCER
HIROYUKI KATO

01:49:54.538 --> 01:49:57.248
CHIEF PRODUCERS
TETSUYA IKEDA, SATOSHI KANNO

01:49:57.338 --> 01:49:59.838
PRODUCERS: TSUTOMU TSUCHIKAWA,
ATSUYUKI SHIMODA

